  "findings": [
    "The optional Root-owned mode authorizes only this Root resource-retirement scope. None and explicit null remain disabled and preserve original raw MetadataFile bytes. Some requires canonical full descriptor bytes. Unknown fields/enum values reject; no new signing credential.",
    "All eight real purpose channels register once. The short admission mutex couples the intent cut with active actual exchanges. Busy refuses immediately under the original 500 ms request; admission remains held through original response/postcheck. Later business entry rejects after intent.",
    "Only exact clean EOF from the same live original peer after authorized intent can return an owned retired channel. Ordinary EOF before intent, partial/malformed frames, peer death, expiry, poison and original errors remain errors. Returned channels are not join proofs.",
    "Actual scoped five-lane, Initial, Learning, Model, Publication, registration and material bridge handles join. Actual owner objects and original listening sockets remain in private bundles; the service is held as the final field. Deadline watcher stops only after the real joined bundle then itself joins.",
    "Root review identified ACK2/OS-exit ordering race against the unchanged client request postcheck. The three-operation correction retains every original request/exchange byte and adds only a consuming one-byte EOF wait on original owner.end. It rejects bytes, refuses peer death, never rearms a request or restores stream.",
    "The final Root response plus original postchecks precede EOF wait while all joined resources remain borrowed and held. A valid daemon must finish ACK2 checks, then release the same actual final stream and aliases while staying alive, before observing Root pidfd. EOF alone proves neither ACK consumption nor C completion.",
    "The original registered writer record does not own its transferred File. Root ACK2 proves no writer-lock release. The actual daemon owns the transferred lock and must independently join and release its consumers and Session.",
    "Nine original whole-file prefixes and legacy serve_deployment body were byte-checked. Original 8627-byte progress prefix and mandatory EOF error remain. Shared Model/publication helpers are deliberate optional-lane changes, with original authority/effect/postchecks retained; they are not claimed byte-identical.",
    "All ten new component sources were read. Four are data/config checks, three actual scoped thread/Unix FD lifetime checks, three actual peer EOF/postcheck/death checks. No component manufactures a valid Root/C/business owner or proves a complete deployment."
  ],
